## Version 0.1.0

o NEW: initial release. Simulation tools moved from {L0ggm} (0.1.3):
  `simulate_sbm()`, `simulate_smallworld()`, `add_population_error()`,
  `smallworldness()`, `proxswap_lattice()`, `categorize()`, and
  `weibull_parameters()`

o NEW: `add_population_error()` gains `method` ("cb" Cudeck & Browne, 1992;
  "tkl" Tucker, Koopman, & Linn, 1969; "wb" Wu & Browne, 2015; "hb" Hu &
  Bentler, 1998), `metric` ("CFI", "TLI", "RMSEA", "SRMR"), and `control`
  arguments. `fit_value` is now a numeric target value (defaults to the
  conventional cutoff of `metric`). `method` has no default and must be
  specified. `metric` defaults to the fit index consistent with `method` ("CFI"
  for "cb" and "tkl", "RMSEA" for "wb", and "SRMR" for "hb"). Errors are always
  limited to the range -1 to 1 and the population correlation matrix with error
  is always positive definite
